  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 221 AM EDT Sun May 10 2026\n\n- Frost/Freeze Next Couple Nights\n\nCanadian surface high builds in tonight with clear skies and light\nwinds leading to frost/freeze conditions for all of the forecast\narea. This should be the coldest night of the week since the sfc\nhigh is moving east Monday night and clouds may be moving in late\nin the night but temperatures could still fall below freezing in \nthe cold spots where winds stay decoupled.\n\n- Rain Chances Tuesday and Late Week\n\nA clipper low moving in the fast northwest flow arrives on Tuesday\nwith the first widespread rain this month. QPF expected to be\naround a quarter inch with some isolated half inch amounts\npossible with scattered convection Tuesday evening.\n\nFlow goes more zonal late week and deeper moisture streams up from\nthe Gulf ahead of a shortwave trough that arrives Friday or\nSaturday with showers and scattered convection.",
